{"stem": "osc", "name": "osc", "description": "Osc\n\nBasic waveform oscillator with a runtime-selectable shape.  Produces a\nfull-scale (\u00b11) signal at the requested frequency; put a `gain` node (or\ncrag.scale) after it to set the level.\n\nAll four shapes share the same frequency and phase inputs, so switching\nthe type while playing stays phase-coherent.  Triangle and square use a\nfixed 0.5 duty cycle (symmetric waveforms).\n\nParameters:\n  type       enum               \u2013 waveform: 0=sine, 1=saw, 2=triangle,\n                                  3=square (default 0 = sine)\n  frequency  [0.1, 20000] Hz    \u2013 oscillation frequency (default 440).\n                                  Sub-audio settings make it usable as an\n                                  audio-rate LFO.\n  phase      [0, 2\u03c0] rad        \u2013 phase offset (default 0)\n\nUsage (after crag.include):\n  %out = crag.subgraph_ref \"osc\"()\n             : () -> !crag.audio<f32, 0, 1>", "sr": 48000, "ch": 1, "build_meta": {"gen_datetime": "2026-07-05 06:16 UTC", "git_commit": "a9ad653", "compiled_with": "768de76"}, "wasm": "osc.wasm", "meta_file": "osc.wasm.cragmeta", "meta": {"schema_version": 1, "sample_rate": 48000, "channels": 1, "parameters": [{"name": "type", "type": "enum", "values": ["sine", "saw", "triangle", "square"], "default": 0, "int_index": 0}, {"name": "frequency", "type": "float", "min": 0.1, "max": 20000.0, "default": 440.0, "unit": "hz", "float_index": 0}, {"name": "phase", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 6.283185, "default": 0.0, "float_index": 1}], "samplers": [], "texture_samplers": [], "events": [], "meters": [{"name": "Output", "type": "float", "min": 0.0, "max": 1.0, "float_index": 0}], "has_visualizer": true, "has_audio_output": true, "viz_width": 512, "viz_height": 256, "compiled_with": "768de76"}, "mca": {"graph": "osc", "block_size": 512, "results": [{"label": "Intel Haswell (x86-64-v3)", "triple": "x86_64-linux-gnu", "march": "x86-64", "mcpu": "haswell"